Z||000000||MR86GT||02-12-2001||02:45 PM||||when I crank up my oil pressure gauge goes to 60# and stays till you stop engine. It does not move when you rev the engine. Can someone help me figure this one out. ||||reg||1
Z||000001||1FST2M6||02-12-2001||03:23 PM||||if your standing near the passengerside door. after removing the grill look just next to the battery near the valve cover.. it's about 2.25"x3" it's black and has one black 3 wire plug on it.. they have a tendency of pluggin up and flaking. check the terminals and the wores for crappy contact or freyed. <P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/sig1fst.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000002||zeusrekning||02-12-2001||07:21 PM||||whohooo another fiero owner in the carolinas <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> <A HREF="http://www.carolinafieros.com" TARGET=_blank>www.carolinafieros.com</A> <BR>it is a v6 right&gt;?||||reg||1
Z||000003||MR86GT||02-12-2001||07:52 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by MR86GT:<BR><B>when I crank up my oil pressure gauge goes to 60# and stays till you stop engine. It does not move when you rev the engine. Can someone help me figure this one out. </B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>I replaced the sending unit with one from another gt and it didnt change a thing. Could be both are bad, but i dont know.<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000004||Phaeton||02-12-2001||09:28 PM||||Like 1FST2M6 said, the wire harness has a tendency to weather right through the weather seal and make cruddy connections.<P>Not that two bad senders in a row is impossible, it just makes the odds better for continuing to look elsewhere.||||reg||12
